From cce748e71e70a5b26da142d133d9c8be1c211fbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <agent@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:07:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: accept the official MCP4725 3-byte fast-mode
 write

The merged 0125 CONTROL_DAC model treated a third byte in a fast-mode
transaction as a NACK, but the official mcp4725 driver writes its full 3-byte
buffer even when only the first two bytes carry the 12-bit value. The frozen
guest driver therefore raised OSError(259) on its first set_raw_value call in
guest evidence. Accept and ignore the trailing fast-mode byte while keeping
the 0x60 EEPROM command decoding unchanged.

No other DAC semantics changed.
---
 hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_controls.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_controls.c b/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_controls.c
index 522c8ec..a8c1691 100644
--- a/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_controls.c
+++ b/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_unit_i2c_controls.c
@@ -1324,6 +1324,11 @@ static int control_send(I2CSlave *dev, uint8_t value)
             if (!s->dac_write_eeprom) { s->dac_raw = s->dac_write_tmp | value; }
             return 0;
         }
+        if (pos >= 2 && !s->dac_write_eeprom) {
+            /* The official driver writes its full 3-byte _BUFFER even for a
+             * fast-mode update; the trailing byte is not part of the command. */
+            return 0;
+        }
         if (pos == 2 && s->dac_write_eeprom) {
             uint16_t value12 = ((s->dac_write_byte1 << 4) | (value >> 4)) & 0x0fff;
             s->dac_raw = value12;
-- 
